@@ -38,6 +38,20 @@ direct library ancestor wins. It does not inspect cwd, `ARCPUZZLES_HOME`,
 arbitrary siblings, or escaping repository/ledger symlinks. Scripts under other
 layouts still need an explicit supported repository root.
 
+For concise authoring coverage, `python3 -m arcpuzzles.review_base_preflight`
+prints job/setting counts, parametric labelled-pair counts, canonical base-pair
+counts, and protected-Racket evaluation counts alongside its receipt path.
+`racket_evaluations` covers the parametric worker; it excludes separate base
+canonical and generation checks. These finite counts do not grant owner
+acceptance or training admission. Full source bindings stay in the receipt.
+For the separate native `arcpuzzles parametric qualify` command, use its existing
+`--summary` option to avoid printing the full source-binding inventory.
+
+The optional witness helper distinguishes output kinds: `review_witness build --out-dir DIR` creates `DIR/witness.json` and `DIR/replay.json`; the legacy
+`build --out DIR` spelling still works. `template --out FILE` writes a recipe
+JSON file, and `check --out FILE` writes a replay JSON file. All outputs must be
+new. These helpers keep their existing source checks and protected execution.
+
 | Use | Entry point | Checks / limits |
 |---|---|---|
 | Observe export sizes and query/demo ratios | `arcpuzzles inspect-export DIR --sizes [--detailed-shapes]` | Verifies artifact hashes/projection, then measures four grid roles and within-episode novel-query counts. Controller-only query-output dimensions; no Racket rerun, token/complexity claim or training admission. [Guide](../../docs/datasets.md#observe-exported-sizes-and-supervision-ratios). |
